<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Three farmers, Akinyi, Otieno and Jepkosgei, paid Ksh <m>{18\,000}</m>, Ksh <m>{24\,000}</m> and Ksh <m>{42\,000}</m> to hire a tractor. They shared the money from their harvest in proportion to what each paid. Akinyi received Ksh <m>{9600}</m>.</p><p>(a) How much money was shared altogether?</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) How much did Jepkosgei receive?</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Sharing in proportion to what each paid means sharing in the ratio of the payments:</p><p><m>{18\,000} : {24\,000} : {42\,000} = {3} : {4} : {7}</m>, which is <m>{14}</m> parts in all.</p><p>(a) Akinyi's <m>{3}</m> parts are Ksh <m>{9600}</m>, so one part is <m>{9600} \div {3} = {3200}</m>. The total is <m>{14} \times {3200} = {44\,800}</m>, so Ksh <m>{44\,800}</m> was shared.</p><p>(b) Jepkosgei receives <m>{7} \times {3200} = {22\,400}</m>, so Ksh <m>{22\,400}</m>.</p><p>Check: Otieno receives <m>{4} \times {3200} = {12\,800}</m>, and <m>{9600} + {12\,800} + {22\,400} = {44\,800}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>44800</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>22400</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>